WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.550
Step six reads the conversions:
each one's target,

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:07.313
its cutover gate, its parallel
run status and its day.

3
00:00:07.313 --> 00:00:09.828
Conversion one, to a managed identity,

4
00:00:09.828 --> 00:00:15.104
is ready to disable its legacy account on
day forty: a clean run past thirty days,

5
00:00:15.104 --> 00:00:18.837
and the owner approved, so it's
the one disable in the plan.

6
00:00:18.837 --> 00:00:24.112
Conversion seven is parallel running,
on day fifteen of thirty, so it waits.

7
00:00:24.112 --> 00:00:27.952
Conversion eight is the warning
sign: on day fifty-nine,

8
00:00:27.952 --> 00:00:33.413
the legacy credential is still in use, so
it isn't clean, and nothing is disabled.

9
00:00:33.413 --> 00:00:35.650
The other five are awaiting cutover.

10
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:40.137
Three of them are blocked by the findings
you just read, and two aren't ready yet.

11
00:00:40.137 --> 00:00:42.301
Notice that a status isn't a write.

12
00:00:42.301 --> 00:00:47.400
Only the plan's three write actions ever
change anything, and only after review.
